course: dictionary
lesson: 15557
title: Supplementary: extra, and supplementary angles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Supplementary means added on to something, to make it bigger, better or complete. Read the clues around the word: «The teacher gave us supplementary questions to try after the test.» The questions come after the main test, so supplementary must mean extra.
explain: Think of supplement, a word you may know, which means something added. Supplementary is the adjective, so it describes a noun: supplementary notes, supplementary work, supplementary information. Test your meaning by swapping in extra: «extra questions to try after the test» still makes sense.
explain: Maths gives the word a special meaning. Two angles are supplementary when they add up to 180 degrees, which makes a straight line. The clues are the numbers and the word angles, so when you see «supplementary angles», think 180.
fact: Supplementary means added on, to make something bigger, better or complete.
fact: Supplementary is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as «supplementary questions».
fact: Supplementary angles add up to 180 degrees and make a straight line.
fact: Complementary angles add up to 90 degrees and make a right angle; do not mix the two words up.
fact: A supplement is something extra added to something else, so the words are related.
exercise: «The teacher gave us supplementary questions to try after the test.» What does supplementary mean here? | Very short and simple | Written in red ink | *Extra, added to the main work | Missing and lost
exercise: Two angles are supplementary. Together they add up to how many degrees? | *180 | 360 | 45 | 90
exercise: «Read the main story, then the supplementary notes at the back.» Find and copy the word that tells you the notes are extra. | back | *supplementary | main | story
test: «Angles a and b are supplementary.» Which pair of angles makes a straight line? | Complementary angles | *Supplementary angles | Right angles | Obtuse angles
test: «The shop gave a supplementary bag of sweets with each box of cards.» What does supplementary mean in this sentence? | Free to the shop owner | *Extra, added on to the box | Heavy | Broken
exam: Which pair is correct: supplementary angles add up to how many degrees, and complementary angles add up to how many degrees? | 360 and 180 | *180 and 90 | 90 and 180 | 180 and 360
